{
  "name": "@wildflowerhealthio/smart-app-react",
  "version": "0.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "description": "The Wildflower chrome every first-party SMART app boots through: `SmartAppRoot` (the launch page for a SMART launch the URL carries, the telemetry consent gate around the launched and standalone branches, one QueryClient, the case latched on mount, the launch-failure banner), `ConnectMenu` (the standalone connect flow: over `fhir-r4-react/smart`'s launch primitives for a SMART app, or through the caller's own sign-in for the Wildflower launcher), the read-status lines an app's page speaks (`LoadingLine`, `LoadingMoreLine`, `ReadFailureLine`), and the in-app patient choice (`usePatientChoice` over `?patient=`, `PatientPicker` with its \"All patients\" row, `PatientChoiceLine` with \"Change patient\"). Built on `fhir-r4-react/smart` for the SMART wiring and `branding-react` for the Wildflower chrome, so neither of those has to know about the other.",
  "type": "module",
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "source": "./src/index.ts",
      "default": "./dist/index.js"
    },
    "./package.json": "./package.json"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "build": "vp pack",
    "check": "vp check",
    "dev": "vp pack --watch",
    "test": "vp test"
  },
